WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.310
In 1968, fishing boats off Newfoundland
landed a record catch of northern cod.

2
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:11.940
By 1992, the spawning stock had
fallen by about 99 per cent.

3
00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:14.050
The fishery was closed.

4
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:19.270
Fish, timber, crops: people take
from nature every single day,

5
00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:20.880
and always will.

6
00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:24.500
So how can people keep taking
food and materials from nature,

7
00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:26.050
without wrecking it?

8
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:30.400
In this mission, you'll see how the ways
people get food and materials can harm

9
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:31.510
wildlife.

10
00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.870
Then you'll find ways to manage that harm,

11
00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.150
so people can keep on taking.

12
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.750
Your mission: find out how people can
keep taking from nature without wrecking

13
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:41.170
it.
